<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to reveal small firms tax package.</title>
<headline>Brazil to reveal small firms tax package.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso was due to announce a tax package for small businesses shortly, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Pedro Malan spent much of the day haggling with congressional representatives of the small companies sector over the plan, thought to propose a flat rate tax of 7.5 percent on firms with annual turnover up to 720,000 reais.</p>
<p>Cardoso was also due to address the nation in a television speech at 2030 local time/2230 GMT, his spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
</text>
